# Financial_SDK/financial_rag_project/user-monitor-sdk — environment reference
#
# ZD-W5-08 · diligence. Generated 2026-09-16 by parsing every `os.getenv` /
# `os.environ` read in the TRACKED Python sources (AST, not grep), then
# classifying each name against what production actually supplies.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in the REQUIRED section. Nothing else needs setting to
# start.
#
# Classification, so the three groups are not guesswork:
#   REQUIRED   read with no USABLE default, and not supplied by the platform.
#              This deliberately includes variables defaulted to "" or None: an
#              empty default is not a working value, it is a missing one with a
#              silent fallback. AUTH0_DOMAIN is read as getenv("AUTH0_DOMAIN",
#              "") -- unset, authentication does not fail loudly, it just never
#              works. Those are the entries most worth setting and the easiest
#              to miss.
#   INJECTED   supplied at runtime -- by the gateway in the Batch/ECS
#              containerOverrides, from Secrets Manager, or by AWS itself. Do
#              NOT set these by hand; listed so you know why they are absent.
#   OPTIONAL   read with a literal default, shown below. Override only to change
#              behaviour.
#
# A note on counts: an earlier survey put this repo at a much larger number of
# keys. That count came from a grep that walked a vendored virtualenv. The
# figures here are from tracked sources only.


# ── REQUIRED (2) ────────────────────────────────────────────
ZENDATA_API_KEY=
ZENDATA_ENGINE_URL=

# ── INJECTED AT RUNTIME (2) — do not set by hand ─────────────
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION
# AWS_REGION

# ── OPTIONAL (2) — default shown ─────────────────────────────
# ZENDATA_EVALUATION_MODE=async
# ZENDATA_LOG_DIR=
